-- title:
--   Relative group law from pinned per-chart addition morphisms
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring that is a Noetherian integral domain and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $R$ satisfying `W.IsElliptic`. Write $E = \mathrm{Proj}$ of the grading induced on $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\ 3)\ R$ modulo the homogeneous ideal generated by the projective Weierstrass polynomial of $W$, with structure morphism $\pi =$ `projModelStrCR` to $\operatorname{Spec} R$ (the canonical map to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the degree-zero part, composed with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $R \to (\text{degree }0)$), and write $\mathcal A_i$ for the homogeneous localisation of that quotient away from the image of the variable $X_i$, an $R$-algebra via the degree-zero part. Assume given, for all $i, j \in \mathrm{Fin}\ 3$, a morphism $\mathrm{pcm}_{ij} \colon \operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal A_i \otimes_R \mathcal A_j) \to E$, and assume that for all $i, j$ and every $l \in \mathrm{Fin}\ 3 \sqcup \mathrm{Fin}\ 3$ the composite of the canonical map $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the localisation of $\mathcal A_i \otimes_R \mathcal A_j$ away from `kw_lrSixU W i j l` into $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal A_i \otimes_R \mathcal A_j)$ with $\mathrm{pcm}_{ij}$ equals `kw_lrSixU_toE W i j l`, i.e. $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the chart comparison ring map followed by the affine inclusion `Proj.awayι` at the degree-one element $X_k$ (with $k$ the index carried by $l$, and the left or right chart map according to the summand). The conclusion is that the type `RelativeGroupLaw R` $\pi$ is nonempty: there is a structure assigning, to every scheme $T$ and every $t \colon T \to \operatorname{Spec} R$, a multiplication, a unit element and an inversion on the set of $\phi \colon T \to E$ with $\phi$ followed by $\pi$ equal to $t$, such that multiplication is associative, the unit is two-sided, inversion is a left inverse, and multiplication commutes with precomposition along any $\psi \colon T' \to T$ with $\psi$ followed by $t$ equal to $t'$.
--
--   This is the assembly step of the construction of the group law on the projective Weierstrass model: it converts a family of per-chart addition morphisms on the nine products of standard affine charts, pinned on the six Lange–Ruppert distinguished opens, into a functorial group law on the relative points of $E$ over $\operatorname{Spec} R$. It is used by [`WeierstrassProjModel.relativeGroupLaw_nonempty_of_thirdLaw_nineCoverage`](thm.html#WeierstrassProjModel.relativeGroupLaw_nonempty_of_thirdLaw_nineCoverage), where the per-chart morphisms are produced from an explicit system of addition laws.
